IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pa14-types`

-- Pensions Act 2014 (UK) — GOAL 1: STATE PENSION (ss 1-5, Schedule 1).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2014-19.txt. The conversion drops
-- the formulas in s 3(2) and Sch 1 paras 4(4) and 7(3) (each N ÷ 35) and the
-- Schedule paragraph numbers.

§ `Goal 1 — state pension`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- N ÷ 35 of a rate, at most the whole of it (35 or more years).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the proportion for` n `years of` rate MEANS
    (`the lesser of` n 35) DIVIDED BY 35 TIMES rate

DECLARE `Kind of state pension` IS ONE OF
    -- s 1(2): reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016.
    `none under this Part (old state pension instead)`
    `none (too few qualifying years)`
    `full rate`
    `reduced rate`
    `transitional rate`

-- s 1(2); s 2(1)-(3) "A person is entitled to a state pension payable at the
-- full rate if— (a) the person has reached pensionable age, and (b) the
-- person has 35 or more qualifying years"; reduced at "at least the minimum
-- number of qualifying years but fewer than 35". s 4(1) "transitional rate
-- if— (a) the person has reached pensionable age, (b) the person has at
-- least the minimum number of qualifying years, and (c) the person has at
-- least one pre-commencement qualifying year"; (3): then not under s 2.
@ref ss 1(2), 2(1)-(3), 4(1)-(3)
@export Which state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 (UK) a person is entitled to on reaching pensionable age: none under this Part if pensionable age was reached before 6 April 2016; transitional rate if they have at least the minimum number of qualifying years and at least one pre-commencement qualifying year; otherwise full rate with 35 or more qualifying years, reduced rate with at least the minimum; otherwise none. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Pension facts`  @desc The day of pensionable age, the qualifying years before and from 6 April 2016, and the minimum
GIVETH A `Kind of state pension`
`the kind of state pension for` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF p's `reaches pensionable age on` LESS THAN Date 6 4 2016 THEN `none under this Part (old state pension instead)`
        IF total LESS THAN p's `minimum qualifying years` THEN `none (too few qualifying years)`
        IF p's `pre-commencement qualifying years` AT LEAST 1 THEN `transitional rate`
        IF total AT LEAST 35 THEN `full rate`
        OTHERWISE `reduced rate`
    WHERE
        total MEANS p's `pre-commencement qualifying years` PLUS p's `post-commencement qualifying years`

-- Sch 1 para 4: Step 2, "(2) If the person has 35 or more pre-commencement
-- qualifying years, ... the full rate of the state pension on 6 April 2016,
-- less (b) any amount to reflect contracting out ... (3) If ... fewer than 35
-- ..., the appropriate proportion of the full rate ..., less" that amount;
-- the appropriate proportion is N ÷ 35.
@ref Sch 1 para 4
GIVEN p IS A `Pension facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the new-system rate for` p MEANS
        `the proportion for` (p's `pre-commencement qualifying years`) `years of` (p's `full rate on 6 April 2016`)
    MINUS p's `contracting-out amount`

-- Sch 1 para 6: "(2) If the amount is equal to or less than the full rate of
-- the state pension on 6 April 2016, the amount is to be revalued in
-- accordance with increases in the full rate ... (3) If the amount is greater
-- ... (a) so much ... as is equal to the full rate ... is to be revalued in
-- accordance with increases in the full rate ..., and (b) so much ... as
-- exceeds the full rate ... in accordance with increases in the general level
-- of prices". (4): by the same percentage as the full rate rose to the day of
-- pensionable age; (5): adding the amount times the revaluing percentage.
@ref Sch 1 para 6
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, p IS A `Pension facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the revalued` amount `for` p MEANS
        `the lesser of` amount r2016 TIMES growth
    PLUS excess PLUS excess TIMES (p's `revaluing percentage for prices` DIVIDED BY 100)
    WHERE
        r2016 MEANS p's `full rate on 6 April 2016`
        growth MEANS p's `full rate at pensionable age` DIVIDED BY r2016
        excess MEANS `the greater of` 0 (amount MINUS r2016)

-- Sch 1 para 2: Step 3, "Take whichever of the rates found under Steps 1 and
-- 2 is higher (the foundation amount)"; Step 4, revalue it.
@ref Sch 1 paras 2-6
@export The amount for a person's pre-commencement qualifying years under Schedule 1 Part 2 to the Pensions Act 2014 (UK): the higher of the old-system rate (Step 1) and the new-system rate (Step 2: N/35 of the full rate on 6 April 2016, less any contracting-out amount), revalued to the day of pensionable age (Step 4: up to the 2016 full rate in line with the full rate, any excess in line with prices). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Pension facts`  @desc The pre-commencement years, the old-system rate, the contracting-out amount, the full rates and the revaluing percentage
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount for pre-commencement qualifying years for` p MEANS
    `the revalued` (`the greater of` (p's `old-system rate`) (`the new-system rate for` p)) `for` p

-- Sch 1 para 7: "(2) If the person has 35 or more post-commencement
-- qualifying years, the amount is equal to the full rate ... on the day on
-- which the person reached pensionable age. (3) If ... fewer than 35 ..., the
-- following proportion" — N ÷ 35.
@ref Sch 1 para 7
GIVEN p IS A `Pension facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount for post-commencement qualifying years for` p MEANS
    `the proportion for` (p's `post-commencement qualifying years`) `years of` (p's `full rate at pensionable age`)

-- s 5(1) "The transitional rate ... is a weekly rate equal to— (a) the sum
-- of the amounts calculated under Schedule 1 for the person's
-- pre-commencement and post-commencement qualifying years capped at the full
-- rate of the state pension on the day on which the person reaches
-- pensionable age, or (b) if higher, the amount for the person's
-- pre-commencement qualifying years alone."
@ref s 5(1)
GIVEN p IS A `Pension facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the transitional rate for` p MEANS
    `the greater of`
        (`the lesser of` (pre PLUS `the amount for post-commencement qualifying years for` p) (p's `full rate at pensionable age`))
        pre
    WHERE
        pre MEANS `the amount for pre-commencement qualifying years for` p

-- s 3(1)-(2): the full rate, and the reduced rate N ÷ 35 of it.
@ref ss 3, 5(1)
@export The weekly rate of the state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 (UK) on reaching pensionable age: the full rate; the reduced rate (qualifying years ÷ 35 of the full rate); the transitional rate (s 5(1) and Schedule 1); or 0 where there is no entitlement under this Part. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Pension facts`  @desc The person's pensionable age, qualifying years and the amounts Schedule 1 needs
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly state pension for` p MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of state pension for` p
    WHEN `full rate` THEN p's `full rate at pensionable age`
    WHEN `reduced rate` THEN `the proportion for` (p's `post-commencement qualifying years`) `years of` (p's `full rate at pensionable age`)
    WHEN `transitional rate` THEN `the transitional rate for` p
    OTHERWISE 0
